# AMD64 thunk export spec -- x3daudio1_7.dll.
#
# From the 2026-08-17 Skyrim Special Edition triage, and the same finding as
# the 2026-08-15 one that added dxgi's and d3d11's: SkyrimSE.exe imports this
# module, Wine provides it as a NATIVE ppc64 builtin, and the loader correctly
# refuses to splice that into a guest call -- reported as c000007b, four times
# over, before the process reaches a single graphics call.  Nothing here is
# hand-written: the export list comes from this module's own .spec.
DLL x3daudio1_7.dll
FROM-SPEC auto

# Without this the module has NO exports at all: x3daudio.h is not in the
# oracle's default translation unit, so both of this module's entry points were
# refused for having no declaration and every guest import of them bound to a
# 0xdead0000 sentinel.  X3DAudioInitialize's second argument is a by-value
# float, which the flat thunk path has carried since cd4ea32c93d.
PROBE-EXTRA x3daudio.h
